      players: '3-8 players; 4-5 is optimal. No permanent partnershipsâ€”high bidder plays against all others.',
      deck: 'Standard 52-card pack. Cards rank A-K-Q-J-10-9-8-7-6-5-4-3-2. Often reduced: 3 players use 20 cards (A-K-Q-J-10), 4 players use 28 (A-8), 5 players use 32 (A-7).',
      equipment: 'Standard deck, poker chips or counters for stakes.',
      dealing: 'Five cards to each playerâ€”either 3 then 2, or 2 then 3. Cards are shuffled only at start and after successful Nap/Wellington/BlÃ¼cher bids; otherwise just gathered and cut.',
